---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'About — x291';
const description = 'About me, my journey into computers, and the things I like to build and understand.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>

  <article class="about">

    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="about__header">
      <span class="annot">about.exe</span>

      <h1>
        A machine I<br />
        never stopped <em>taking apart.</em>
      </h1>

      <p class="lede">
        I got introduced to computers when I was six.
        I never really left.
      </p>
    </header>


    <!-- Origin -->
    <section class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter__meta">
        <span>01</span>
        <span>ORIGIN</span>
      </div>

      <div class="chapter__body">
        <p>
          My first encounter with a computer happened at an early age,
          around six years old. From then on, computers became part of
          my everyday life.
        </p>

        <p>
          At first, I was simply using them. Games, software, the
          internet — whatever was interesting at the time. But eventually
          a different question started appearing:
        </p>

        <blockquote>
          <span>“</span>
          <p>How does this thing actually work?</p>
        </blockquote>

        <p>
          That question turned out to be considerably more interesting
          than the answers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- Obsession -->
    <section class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter__meta">
        <span>02</span>
        <span>OBSESSION</span>
      </div>

      <div class="chapter__body">
        <p>
          My interest in computers eventually became an interest in
          <strong>computing itself</strong>.
        </p>

        <p>
          I wanted to understand what happens underneath the abstractions:
          how programs communicate with an operating system, how memory
          is organized, how a CPU executes instructions, how networks
          move information, and why seemingly simple things are built
          the way they are.
        </p>

        <p>
          <em>Mr. Robot</em> played a surprisingly large part in that.
          It made computers feel less like appliances and more like
          machines worth understanding.
        </p>

        <p>
          And, honestly, my ADHD brain probably didn't help.
          It has a habit of finding something interesting and then
          immediately asking:
        </p>

        <div class="terminal">
          <div class="terminal__bar">
            <span></span>
            <span></span>
            <span></span>
          </div>

          <div class="terminal__body">
            <span class="prompt">$</span>
            <span>why?</span>
            <span class="cursor">_</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="soft">
          Then another question appears. And another.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- What I do -->
    <section class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter__meta">
        <span>03</span>
        <span>INTERESTS</span>
      </div>

      <div class="chapter__body">
        <p>
          These days, I'm particularly interested in the parts of
          computing that expose what's underneath the surface.
        </p>

        <div class="interests">
          <div class="interest">
            <span class="interest__number">01</span>
            <h2>Systems</h2>
            <p>
              Operating systems, computer architecture, networking,
              low-level programming, and the boundary between software
              and hardware.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="interest">
            <span class="interest__number">02</span>
            <h2>Programming</h2>
            <p>
              I enjoy learning languages and building things with them,
              especially when doing so reveals a different way of
              thinking about software.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="interest">
            <span class="interest__number">03</span>
            <h2>Mathematics</h2>
            <p>
              Discrete mathematics, logic, algorithms, and the mathematical
              ideas that quietly sit underneath computer science.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="interest">
            <span class="interest__number">04</span>
            <h2>Writing</h2>
            <p>
              Writing about what I learn forces me to understand it
              properly. That's why I keep a technical blog.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>


    <!-- Philosophy -->
    <section class="chapter chapter--last">
      <div class="chapter__meta">
        <span>04</span>
        <span>NOW</span>
      </div>

      <div class="chapter__body">
        <p>
          I don't think my goal is to learn everything about computers.
          That's impossible.
        </p>

        <p>
          What interests me is following the questions far enough
          that the abstraction disappears.
        </p>

        <blockquote class="final-quote">
          <p>
            I like knowing what is happening underneath.
          </p>
        </blockquote>

        <div class="about__links">
          <a href="/projects">Explore my projects <span>→</span></a>
          <a href="/articles">Read what I've learned <span>→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </article>

</BaseLayout>


<style>
  .about {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .about__header {
    padding: 1rem 0 5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .about__header h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 8vw, 5rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
  }

  .about__header h1 em {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 38ch;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .chapter {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 6rem 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: 4rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .chapter__meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    padding-top: 0.45rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .chapter__meta span:first-child {
    color: var(--mark);
  }

  .chapter__body {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .chapter__body > p {
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
  }

  .chapter__body > p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .chapter__body strong {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  blockquote {
    position: relative;
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--mark);
    background: var(--paper-raised);
  }

  blockquote span {
    position: absolute;
    top: -0.8rem;
    left: 1rem;
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 3rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--mark);
  }

  blockquote p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .terminal {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--paper-raised);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .terminal__bar {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .terminal__bar span {
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--ink-soft);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .terminal__body {
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  .prompt {
    margin-right: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--mark);
  }

  .cursor {
    margin-left: 0.2rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    animation: blink 1.1s steps(2, start) infinite;
  }

  .soft {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .interests {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1px;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .interest {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--paper);
  }

  .interest__number {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--mark);
  }

  .interest h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .interest p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .chapter--last {
    border-bottom: 0;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .final-quote {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    border-left: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: transparent;
    padding: 2rem 0;
  }

  .final-quote p {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .about__links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .about__links a {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink-soft);
    padding-bottom: 0.15rem;
  }

  .about__links a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .about__links span {
    color: var(--mark);
  }

  @keyframes blink {
    50% {
      opacity: 0;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .about__header {
      padding-bottom: 3.5rem;
    }

    .chapter {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
      padding: 3rem 0;
    }

    .chapter__meta {
      flex-direction: row;
      gap: 0.75rem;
    }

    .interests {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
